{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Cartographer's Algorithm","logline":"When cartographer Veya builds an algorithm that predicts how the isles drift and which skybridges will fail, Drift Cartel toll-master Kael moves to bury it and seize the last stable routes, and she must prove it publicly before the archipelago is cut apart.","theme":"Truths are safer shared than hoarded.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Pattern in the Drift","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_prediction","title":"The First Prediction","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya runs her late mentor's drift model against her own wind-sight readings and the algorithm correctly forecasts a skybridge shift. The model shows the isles drifting apart and several bridges failing.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Validate the algorithm against live bridge movement.","conflict":"The academy's senior cartographers dismiss the model as her mentor's discredited theory, and Veya's stubbornness makes her refuse to recheck a doubtful reading.","outcome":"The prediction proves correct, but she hides a flawed data point and resolves to chart a safe route before going public."},{"id":"scn_docks_ledger","title":"The Toll-Master's Ledger","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael notices that shipping insurers and wind-debt records are shifting in ways that suggest a failing network. He hears that a Silverspine cartographer is charting bridge movement.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Secure the Cartel's monopoly on the last stable skybridge routes before the bridges collapse.","conflict":"Cartel princes want proof of collapse before they commit, and Kael cannot act on rumour without exposing his own fears.","outcome":"Kael decides to find and control Veya's charts, treating them as an asset to seize."},{"id":"scn_kael_offer","title":"An Offer Between Rivals","summary":"Kael travels to Silverspine and offers his old fellow apprentice a patron's funding in exchange for exclusive rights to her charts. Veya sees the offer for what it is and refuses.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to buy exclusive control of the charts; Veya wants to keep them independent.","conflict":"Kael admires her skill but cannot let her succeed on her own terms, and Veya craves recognition enough to be tempted.","outcome":"Veya refuses, and Kael leaves with a quiet threat and a view of her unfinished work.","depends_on":["scn_docks_ledger","scn_silverspine_prediction"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Closing Lanes","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_levy","title":"Grain and Whispers","summary":"Veya travels to The Hollow to test her predictions against the windmill isles. Maris is smuggling grain around the Cartel levy and recognises Veya's tools as something that could expose the cartel.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants corroborating drift data; Maris wants to keep The Hollow fed despite the levy.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya is a Cartel spy after Kael's visit.","outcome":"Maris tests Veya with a hard bargain, and they agree to trade wind-current knowledge for her service corridors.","depends_on":["scn_kael_offer"]},{"id":"scn_corridor_run","title":"The Service Corridors","summary":"Maris guides Veya through unmapped service corridors between windmills and granaries to reach a remote bridge anchor. Veya's wind-sight reads the anchor's drift and confirms the algorithm.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Collect a bridge-anchor measurement without being seen by Cartel enforcers.","conflict":"Cartel enforcers are closing in on Maris's smuggling routes, and Veya's refusal to admit an error nearly leads them down a dead corridor.","outcome":"They obtain the measurement and escape, and Veya starts to rely on Maris.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_levy"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_sabotage","title":"Cables That Would Not Hold","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya warns the Bridge Wardens that braided cloudstone cables will fail within weeks. She finds that supplies for the forge-island have been quietly short, and the Wardens blame Kael.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants the Wardens to reinforce failing bridges; Kael wants to keep the Wardens too weak to contest Cartel control of the routes.","conflict":"Kael smoothly denies sabotage, and the Wardens will not act on an unpublished model.","outcome":"The Wardens agree to a public demonstration, but Kael learns the date and place.","depends_on":["scn_corridor_run"]},{"id":"scn_docks_suppression","title":"The Cartel Closes Ranks","summary":"Kael persuades the Cartel to bar Veya's charts from the shipping lanes and to enforce wind-debt claims against her allies. Maris is identified as the smuggler behind The Hollow's grain.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to cut off Veya's access to data; Maris wants to deliver grain to The Hollow.","conflict":"Maris is caught between loyalty to home and her friendship with Veya, and Kael uses his ledger-mastery to find the weakest point in her arrangements.","outcome":"Maris escapes with part of her cargo, but the Cartel now holds her routes and the wind-debt on Veya.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_sabotage"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_betrayal","title":"A Flaw Exposed","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Kael's agents publicly challenge the model by pointing to the flawed data point Veya hid. She cannot admit the error, and the academy suspends her access to the charts.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to defend the algorithm; Kael wants to discredit it before the demonstration.","conflict":"Veya's inability to admit a mistake turns a small error into a scandal.","outcome":"Veya is stripped of academy access, and Maris arrives with the measurement Veya needs to correct the model.","depends_on":["scn_docks_suppression","scn_silverspine_prediction"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Public Proof","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_correction","title":"Admitting the Error","summary":"Veya shelters in The Hollow with Maris. She finally admits her mistake and rebuilds the algorithm using Maris's corridor data, producing a model that holds.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Rebuild a sound model and decide to publish rather than hoard it.","conflict":"Veya's pride resists the correction, and Maris must decide whether to forgive her and risk her isle.","outcome":"The corrected algorithm predicts a collapse at Mistral Docks, and Maris commits to helping Veya reach the demonstration.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_betrayal","scn_corridor_run"]},{"id":"scn_mistral_demonstration","title":"The Demonstration at Mistral Docks","summary":"Veya publishes the model before the Cartel's assembled merchants and names a bridge that will fail within the hour. Kael tries to halt the demonstration and push her out of the Docks.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to prove the prediction publicly; Kael wants to stop it and seize the stable routes.","conflict":"Kael invokes Cartel charter authority and wind-debt claims, while the bridge's failure would endanger merchants who have no reason to trust Veya.","outcome":"The bridge fails exactly as predicted, and the merchants see the model is right.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_correction"]},{"id":"scn_kael_choice","title":"The Price of Control","summary":"With the network failing, Kael realises that hoarding the last stable routes would cost the Cartel more than sharing the charts. He must choose between his monopoly and the merchants' survival.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to secure the stable routes; Veya wants him to open the charts to everyone.","conflict":"Kael equates price with worth and cannot easily accept that control is not worth the cost.","outcome":"Kael yields, releasing the charts to the shipping lanes and the Wardens.","depends_on":["scn_mistral_demonstration"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"A Shared Map","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_rebuild","title":"Braiding the New Routes","summary":"The Bridge Wardens at Emberroost use the shared charts to reinforce failing cables and reroute traffic. Kael's Cartel supplies materials in an uneasy truce, and the wind-debt on Veya's allies is eased.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Reinforce the bridges and reroute traffic safely.","conflict":"Old resentments between Wardens and Cartel threaten the cooperation, and Kael's pride resists working under Warden direction.","outcome":"The key routes stabilise, and Kael accepts shared governance of the toll lanes.","depends_on":["scn_kael_choice"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"The Quiet Isle Fed","summary":"The Grain Levy is eased in exchange for open charts and safe shipping, and Maris no longer has to smuggle. She forgives Veya, though slowly, and recognises that sometimes hiding is as brave as standing still.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Secure The Hollow's grain deliveries and mend the friendship.","conflict":"Maris's reluctance to forgive and trust competes with the relief of the lifted levy.","outcome":"The Hollow is fed, and Maris and Veya renew their alliance.","depends_on":["scn_kael_choice"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_legacy","title":"The Mentor's Theory Vindicated","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya's mentor's theory is formally recognised, and she shares the algorithm openly with the next generation of cartographers. She credits Maris and acknowledges her own error.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Record the algorithm for public use and honour her mentor.","conflict":"Her craving for recognition tempts her to claim the work alone, but she chooses to share credit.","outcome":"The charts become a shared public archive, and Veya embraces openness over hoarding.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_rebuild","scn_hollow_harvest"]}]}]}
</Output>
