 into a scandal.","outcome":"Veya is stripped of academy access, and Maris arrives with the measurement Veya needs to correct the model.","depends_on":["scn_docks_suppression","scn_silverspine_prediction"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Public Proof","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_correction","title":"Admitting the Error","summary":"Veya shelters in The Hollow with Maris. She finally admits her mistake and rebuilds the algorithm using Maris's corridor data, producing a model that holds.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Rebuild a sound model and decide to publish rather than hoard it.","conflict":"Veya's pride resists the correction, and Maris must decide whether to forgive her and risk her isle.","outcome":"The corrected algorithm predicts a collapse at Mistral Docks, and Maris commits to helping Veya reach the demonstration.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_betrayal","scn_corridor_run"]},{"id":"scn_mistral_demonstration","title":"The Demonstration at Mistral Docks","summary":"Veya publishes the model before the Cartel's assembled merchants and names a bridge that will fail within the hour. Kael tries to halt the demonstration and push her out of the Docks.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to prove the prediction publicly; Kael wants to stop it and seize the stable routes.","conflict":"Kael invokes Cartel charter authority and wind-debt claims, while the bridge's failure would endanger merchants who have no reason to trust Veya.","outcome":"The bridge fails exactly as predicted, and the merchants see the model is right.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_correction"]},{"id":"scn_kael_choice","title":"The Price of Control","summary":"With the network failing, Kael realises that hoarding the last stable routes would cost the Cartel more than sharing the charts. He must choose between his monopoly and the merchants' survival.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to secure the stable routes; Veya wants him to open the charts to everyone.","conflict":"Kael equates price with worth and cannot easily accept that control is not worth the cost.","outcome":"Kael yields, releasing the charts to the shipping lanes and the Wardens.","depends_on":["scn_mistral_demonstration"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"A Shared Map","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_rebuild","title":"Braiding the New Routes","summary":"The Bridge Wardens at Emberroost use the shared charts to reinforce failing cables and reroute traffic. Kael's Cartel supplies materials in an uneasy truce, and the wind-debt on Veya's allies is eased.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Reinforce the bridges and reroute traffic safely.","conflict":"Old resentments between Wardens and Cartel threaten the cooperation, and Kael's pride resists working under Warden direction.","outcome":"The key routes stabilise, and Kael accepts shared governance of the toll lanes.","depends_on":["scn_kael_choice"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"The Quiet Isle Fed","summary":"The Grain Levy is eased in exchange for open charts and safe shipping, and Maris no longer has to smuggle. She forgives Veya, though slowly, and recognises that sometimes hiding is as brave as standing still.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Secure The Hollow's grain deliveries and mend the friendship.","conflict":"Maris's reluctance to forgive and trust competes with the relief of the lifted levy.","outcome":"The Hollow is fed, and Maris and Veya renew their alliance.","depends_on":["scn_kael_choice"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_legacy","title":"The Mentor's Theory Vindicated","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya's mentor's theory is formally recognised, and she shares the algorithm openly with the next generation of cartographers. She credits Maris and acknowledges her own error.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Record the algorithm for public use and honour her mentor.","conflict":"Her craving for recognition tempts her to claim the work alone, but she chooses to share credit.","outcome":"The charts become a shared public archive, and Veya embraces openness over hoarding.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_rebuild","scn_hollow_harvest"]}]}]}
