d staying hidden with Veya.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to seize the grain stores; Maris wants to protect her isle.","conflict":"Maris's loyalty to home conflicts with her friendship with Veya, and Kael's levy is legal under Cartel charter but ruinous for the Hollow.","outcome":"Maris reveals herself to negotiate and Kael takes half the stores, but he sees how much the isle sacrifices and is unsettled.","depends_on":["scn_the_corridor_chase"]},{"id":"scn_the_charts_shared","title":"Truth at Silverspine","summary":"Veya and Maris return to Silverspine and Veya shows the Academy and the Wardens her full charts, admitting they are incomplete. The Wardens confirm the isles are drifting apart and the best routes are failing.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Get the charts verified and shared with the Bridge Wardens.","conflict":"Veya must admit her mentor's theory was only partly right, which wounds her pride, and the Wardens distrust a Hollow smuggler in their halls.","outcome":"The Wardens accept the charts and agree to rebuild a single route, but need the Cartel's lanes and Kael's cooperation, which leads to a showdown.","depends_on":["scn_the_hollow_burns_a_silo"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Bridge","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_toll_standoff","title":"Standoff at Mistral Docks","summary":"Veya and Maris bring the charts to Mistral Docks. Kael stands to seize the last stable route, but the charts show it will fail within days, and that only a joint crossing can save the isles.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Convince Kael to open the Cartel's lanes and join the rebuilding of the last route.","conflict":"Kael admires Veya's work yet cannot let her succeed, and his belief in price over worth makes him doubt the offer is free.","outcome":"Kael tests the charts himself, sees the failing bridge is real, and agrees to a joint crossing, but only if he can oversee it.","depends_on":["scn_the_charts_shared"]},{"id":"scn_the_crossing","title":"Weaving the Last Bridge","summary":"At Emberroost, Wardens braid new cloudstone cable while Veya reads the wind, Maris guides the crews through the unmapped corridors, and Kael releases Cartel supplies. A spark threatens to sever the bridge, and all three must act together.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Complete the last safe skybridge route before the current fails.","conflict":"Open flame is forbidden aloft and a single spark can sever a skybridge, while each of the three must overcome their own flaw to trust the others.","outcome":"Kael spends his own ledger holdings to save the bridge, Veya yields the lead to Maris's route, and the crossing holds.","depends_on":["scn_the_toll_standoff"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"Shared Wind","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_pays_the_debt","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael faces the Cartel's princes, who are furious at his spending. He argues that control cost more than it gained and renegotiates the tolls and the grain levy.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Persuade the Cartel to lower tolls and ease the grain levy.","conflict":"The Cartel's princes still equate profit with worth and threaten to cast him out.","outcome":"Kael wins a reduced toll and levy, at the cost of his standing, and begins to repay his wind-debt in labour.","depends_on":["scn_the_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_maris_comes_home","title":"Bread for the Hollow","summary":"Maris returns to The Hollow with the eased levy and openly shares the secret silo routes with the Wardens, deciding that hiding can be as brave as standing still, and so can trusting.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Secure The Hollow's grain supply under the new levy.","conflict":"Her people fear that sharing the routes will expose them again, and Maris must forgive Kael's earlier levy.","outcome":"The Hollow Circle accepts the arrangement, and Maris takes on a new role as a trusted guide between isles.","depends_on":["scn_kael_pays_the_debt"]},{"id":"scn_veya_publishes_the_charts","title":"Charts for Everyone","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya publishes the complete charts openly, crediting Maris, the Wardens and her late mentor, and Kael attends to repay his wind-debt in labour, a wary rival turned ally.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Share the charts so every isle can navigate the changing skybridges.","conflict":"Veya must give up sole recognition, and doubts linger over whether Kael can be trusted.","outcome":"The charts are shared across the archipelago, the three part with a fragile trust, and the isles begin to adapt to the drift together.","depends_on":["scn_maris_comes_home"]}]}]}
