{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Grain and the Map","logline":"When Veya's new charts reveal the skybridges are failing, she must publish the truth while Maris smuggles grain past the Cartel levy and Kael moves to destroy both to protect his monopoly and the fragile peace.","theme":"Truth shared is safer than truth hoarded","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Fraying Map","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_veya_charts_the_break","title":"The Colours of Failing Wind","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya reads the wind currents and discovers that the stable skybridge routes are collapsing faster than anyone admits, confirming her late mentor's theory that the isles are drifting apart.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Chart a safe route through the breaking skybridge network and confirm her mentor's theory.","conflict":"Her wind-sight shows the data is alarming, but her stubbornness makes her refuse to share unfinished charts with academy colleagues who urge caution.","outcome":"Veya completes a draft chart showing the last stable routes, and resolves to keep it secret until it is perfect."},{"id":"scn_kael_tallies_the_tolls","title":"The Weakest Point","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael audits the Cartel's ledgers and uses his ledger-mastery to identify the stable routes that will survive the collapse, planning to seize them before anyone else learns of the danger.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Seize the last stable skybridge routes to secure the Cartel's monopoly.","conflict":"Without accurate charts he cannot tell which routes will last, and he equates price with worth, so his attempts to buy the information are blunt.","outcome":"Kael learns that Veya is charting the network and decides her work must be acquired or buried.","depends_on":["scn_veya_charts_the_break"]},{"id":"scn_maris_counts_the_silos","title":"The Levy Arrives","summary":"In The Hollow, Cartel assessors announce the grain levy and Maris sees the isle's stores will not survive it, so she begins planning to move grain through secret silos and service corridors.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Protect The Hollow by smuggling enough grain to keep it fed.","conflict":"The Hollow Circle's elders fear open defiance, and Cartel enforcers are already watching the docks.","outcome":"Maris secretly diverts her first cart of grain and realises she needs charts of the shifting bridges to move it safely."},{"id":"scn_veya_meets_maris","title":"Trading Paths for Currents","summary":"Veya travels to The Hollow seeking a safe overland path for her survey, and meets Maris. They agree to trade wind-current knowledge for Maris's unmapped service corridors.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants access to secret paths for her survey; Maris wants bridge forecasts for smuggling.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya is a Cartel informant, while Veya hides how much her charts reveal.","outcome":"They form an uneasy alliance, and Maris learns the isles are drifting apart.","depends_on":["scn_veya_charts_the_break","scn_maris_counts_the_silos"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Pressure on Every Bridge","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_offers_a_bargain","title":"A Charming Offer","summary":"Kael travels to Silverspine and offers Veya a generous price for her charts, appealing to their shared past as apprentices.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to buy Veya's charts; Veya wants to learn how much the Cartel knows.","conflict":"Kael admires her skill but cannot let her succeed, while Veya refuses to let him control her work and cannot admit that his figures on bridge failure match hers.","outcome":"Veya refuses, and Kael leaves with a veiled threat and the knowledge that she is working with someone from The Hollow.","depends_on":["scn_kael_tallies_the_tolls","scn_veya_meets_maris"]},{"id":"scn_smuggling_run_to_the_docks","title":"The Night Run","summary":"Maris guides Veya through service corridors and bridges to carry grain to Mistral Docks, where hungry traders are waiting to buy.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Deliver the grain to buyers and return unseen.","conflict":"Cartel enforcers close in on the route, and Veya's insistence on checking a bridge reading against her chart nearly gets them caught.","outcome":"They deliver the grain but an enforcer sees Maris's face, and the Cartel now knows who is smuggling.","depends_on":["scn_kael_offers_a_bargain"]},{"id":"scn_wardens_accuse_kael","title":"Smoke Over Emberroost","summary":"At Emberroost, Bridge Wardens confront Kael with proof that Cartel shipments of braiding supplies were sabotaged, and Veya arrives to ask them to endorse her charts.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants the Wardens' backing; Kael wants to deflect blame and discredit her charts.","conflict":"The Wardens demand proof, and Kael turns the wind-debt rule against Veya, exposing that her unfinished charts are unverified.","outcome":"The Wardens agree to examine the charts only if Veya publishes in full, while Kael quietly orders enforcers to move on The Hollow.","depends_on":["scn_kael_offers_a_bargain"]},{"id":"scn_maris_betrayed_by_pride","title":"The Silo Raid","summary":"Enforcers raid The Hollow's hidden silos, burning stores and detaining millers, and Maris learns that Veya's delay in sharing her route data exposed the corridors.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Save what grain remains and protect the millers.","conflict":"Maris's loyalty to home collides with her friendship with Veya, and Veya cannot admit her delay was the cause.","outcome":"Maris breaks with Veya and takes the remaining grain alone, leaving Veya without her ally.","depends_on":["scn_wardens_accuse_kael","scn_smuggling_run_to_the_docks"]},{"id":"scn_veya_confronts_her_flaw","title":"The Mentor's Last Note","summary":"Alone at Silverspine, Veya rereads her mentor's notes and finds that his theory was incomplete and that her own chart contains an error that endangered Maris.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Correct her charts and decide whether to publish them.","conflict":"Admitting error threatens the recognition she craves and her fear of becoming like the Cartel leaders.","outcome":"Veya admits she was wrong, corrects the charts, and decides to publish them openly and to seek Maris's forgiveness.","depends_on":["scn_maris_betrayed_by_pride"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Stable Bridge","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_publication_at_the_docks","title":"Publishing the Truth","summary":"Veya posts the corrected charts at Mistral Docks before the assembled merchants just as Maris arrives with the last grain shipment, and Kael steps in to stop them both.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants the truth published; Maris needs the grain delivered; Kael wants both destroyed to keep order.","conflict":"Kael uses his ledger-mastery to threaten merchants with wind-debt calls unless they surrender the charts and grain, while Maris's distrust of Veya wavers.","outcome":"Maris chooses to trust Veya, and together they expose Kael's sabotage and his own ledgers, forcing the merchants to read the charts.","depends_on":["scn_veya_confronts_her_flaw","scn_maris_betrayed_by_pride","scn_wardens_accuse_kael"]},{"id":"scn_kael_faces_the_cost","title":"Control Costs More","summary":"With the merchants turning against him, Kael moves to cut the main skybridge cable to stop the charts spreading, and Veya's wind-sight lets her warn the crowd away as Maris guides them through a service corridor.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to silence the charts; Veya and Maris want everyone off the failing bridge.","conflict":"Kael's act would strand the docks and collapse the trade he hoped to own, and he must weigh price against lives.","outcome":"Kael stands down and the bridge holds, his monopoly lost and his hold on the Cartel broken.","depends_on":["scn_publication_at_the_docks"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What the Drift Leaves","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_wardens_adopt_the_charts","title":"A Shared Chart","summary":"At Emberroost the Bridge Wardens adopt Veya's charts and begin reinforcing the stable routes, giving credit to Maris's corridors as well.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Turn the published charts into a plan to save the bridge network.","conflict":"The Wardens, wary after the Toll War, resist working with a smuggler, and Veya must share credit she once wanted for herself.","outcome":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle agree to a joint plan, and Veya gives Maris equal credit.","depends_on":["scn_kael_faces_the_cost"]},{"id":"scn_kael_answers_for_the_levy","title":"The Ledger Balanced","summary":"Kael, stripped of his tolls, meets Veya and Maris and agrees to open the Cartel's ledgers and ease the grain levy as repayment of his debt.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Settle what Kael owes The Hollow and the Wardens.","conflict":"Maris rarely forgives, and Kael still struggles to value anything beyond its price.","outcome":"The levy is cut, Maris grants a wary truce, and Kael accepts that control cost him more than it gained.","depends_on":["scn_kael_faces_the_cost","scn_wardens_adopt_the_charts"]},{"id":"scn_harvest_on_the_hollow","title":"Windmills Turning","summary":"Back in The Hollow, the mills grind grain freely, and Veya returns to hand Maris a copy of the final charts as the isles keep drifting.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Repair their friendship and secure the Hollow's future.","conflict":"The isles are still drifting apart, and Maris must decide whether she can forgive Veya fully.","outcome":"Maris forgives Veya, both accept that sharing truth and hiding it each take courage, and they plan the next survey together.","depends_on":["scn_kael_answers_for_the_levy"]}]}]}
