eya's wind-sight will time the crossings and Maris's corridors will hide the route, but the combined map shows the failing bridges converge on Emberroost.","depends_on":["scn_docks_meeting","scn_hollow_levy"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_forge","title":"The Braiding Pits","summary":"Veya and Maris travel to Emberroost, where the Bridge Wardens braid cloudstone cable, and discover that supplies for the forge-island have been sabotaged.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"They want the Wardens to reinforce the failing bridges along their charted route.","conflict":"The Wardens accuse the Cartel of sabotage but cannot repair anything without cloudstone, and the wind-debt rule means every crossing the pair makes adds to what they owe.","outcome":"The Wardens agree to braid new cable if cloudstone stock and grain for the forge crews can be delivered, tying the three threads together; Veya must admit her chart needs Maris's grain routes.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_meeting"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_betrayal","title":"A Chart Taken","summary":"Returning to Silverspine for the final bridge readings, Veya finds her mentor's notes missing; Kael, using the Academy's debts as leverage, has already copied them.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants her mentor's notes to complete the route; Kael wants to secure the charts before the Wardens can use them.","conflict":"Veya's refusal to admit she was wrong to travel openly gave Kael the opening, and his admiration for her skill clashes with his need to stop her.","outcome":"Kael takes the notes and moves Cartel enforcers onto the stable routes, while Veya, shaken, understands that hoarding the truth is what left it exposed.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_forge"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_choice","title":"Hiding as Bravery","summary":"Cartel enforcers close on The Hollow; Maris must choose between guarding her isle's grain and joining Veya's plan, and decides to open her secret silos to the Wardens' supply run.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants to protect The Hollow while keeping her promise to Veya.","conflict":"Her loyalty to home pulls against her friendship, and her habit of unforgiving distrust makes her doubt Veya after the stolen notes.","outcome":"Maris forgives Veya, loads grain into the hidden corridors, and prepares the crossing that will meet Kael on the last stable bridge.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_betrayal"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Bridge","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_docks_confrontation","title":"The Weakest Point","summary":"At Mistral Docks, the three converge: Veya's charts, Maris's grain, and Kael's ledger are all needed to open the failing route, and Kael tries to claim the crossing as Cartel property.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to cross with grain and cable to save the bridges; Kael wants to seize the last stable routes for the Cartel.","conflict":"Kael's ledger-mastery exposes the weak point in their arrangement, and Veya's pride and Maris's distrust nearly split the pair apart.","outcome":"Veya admits her chart is wrong where Kael's records are right, Kael sees that holding the routes alone would let them collapse, and the three agree to weave their knowledge into one crossing.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_choice","scn_silverspine_betrayal"]},{"id":"scn_last_crossing","title":"The Weaving Crossing","summary":"The three work the failing bridge together, with Veya reading the wind, Maris guiding the grain through hidden corridors, and Kael's ledger settling the wind-debt, while the Wardens braid fresh cable.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Complete the crossing and re-anchor the bridge before it breaks.","conflict":"A stray spark from a cheap Cartel lantern threatens to sever the cable, forcing all three to act in concert under the no-open-flame rule.","outcome":"The bridge holds, the threads of map, grain, and ledger bind into one working route, and Kael gives up his claim to exclusive control.","depends_on":["scn_docks_confrontation"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Pattern Holds","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_ledgers_settled","title":"Debts Repaid","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael opens the Cartel's ledgers, cancels the grain levy for The Hollow, and agrees to share toll revenue with the Wardens in exchange for labour on the bridges.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to repair what his control cost; Maris wants the levy lifted.","conflict":"Maris cannot easily forgive the Cartel, and Kael must give up the monopoly he built his life around.","outcome":"The levy is lifted and the toll war ends in a fragile truce, with Kael accepting that control costs more than it gains.","depends_on":["scn_last_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_charts_shared","title":"Charts Shared","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine and publishes the complete chart of the skybridge network, crediting Maris and Kael, and the Academy copies it for every isle.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to prove her mentor's theory and make the charts safe for all.","conflict":"Her old need for sole recognition tempts her to withhold credit, and she must admit she was wrong about hoarding.","outcome":"Veya shares the charts freely, the isles prepare for their slow drift apart, and she is honoured for the work rather than the claim.","depends_on":["scn_last_crossing","scn_ledgers_settled"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"The Quiet Harvest","summary":"Back home on The Hollow, Maris and Veya share the first open harvest, and the windmills turn grain for the whole archipelago without hiding.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris wants to see her isle fed openly; Veya and Kael come to repay what they owe.","conflict":"Old distrust lingers between Maris and Kael, and Kael must pay his wind-debt in labour among the people he once taxed.","outcome":"The three stand together as the windmills turn, the threads of map, grain, and ledger woven into a lasting peace.","depends_on":["scn_ledgers_settled","scn_charts_shared"]}]}]}
