id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants Veya to hand over or license her charts; Veya wants to learn how much he already knows.","conflict":"Kael's offer would give Veya the recognition she craves, but she fears becoming like the Cartel's ambitious leaders.","outcome":"Veya refuses, but her refusal confirms to Kael that the map exists, and he leaves with a veiled threat.","depends_on":["scn_discovery_at_silverspine","scn_kael_hears_rumour"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Breaking Bridges","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_warning","title":"Cables That Fray","summary":"Veya goes to Emberroost to ask the Bridge Wardens whether the chart's predicted failures match their cable inspections. They do, and the Wardens say Cartel-delayed supplies are making repairs impossible.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to test the map's predictions against real skybridge conditions using her wind-sight.","conflict":"The Wardens suspect the Cartel of sabotage and distrust any chart that might give the Cartel an advantage, and Veya cannot admit she misread one bridge's drift.","outcome":"Veya's wind-sight confirms the map's forecast and she learns one key bridge will fail within weeks, which raises the stakes of keeping the map secret.","depends_on":["scn_kael_offers_bargain"]},{"id":"scn_cartel_tightens","title":"The Toll Is Raised","summary":"Kael raises skybridge tolls and has enforcers watch Silverspine, while pressing the Hollow's grain shipments with a levy. Maris's smuggling routes come under pressure.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to squeeze every route into Cartel control; Maris wants to get grain past the levy to The Hollow.","conflict":"Maris is nearly caught by enforcers, and Kael's pragmatism makes him dismiss the toll's human cost.","outcome":"Maris escapes with a ledger fragment showing Kael is hunting a map, and she decides to find the cartographer who holds it.","depends_on":["scn_kael_offers_bargain"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_alliance","title":"Windmill Corridors","summary":"Maris brings Veya to The Hollow and shows her the unmapped service corridors between windmills. Veya trades her wind-current knowledge for Maris's secret paths.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants a safe route that avoids the failing bridges; Maris wants protection for the grain smuggling.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly, and Veya's secrecy about the full map makes Maris suspect she is holding something back.","outcome":"They form an uneasy alliance and discover that Maris's corridors fill gaps in the map, giving Veya a route that might work.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_warning","scn_cartel_tightens"]},{"id":"scn_enforcers_raid","title":"Smoke Over the Silo","summary":"Kael's enforcers track Maris to The Hollow and raid the grain silos, forcing Veya and Maris to flee along the service corridors with the map.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to seize the map and break Maris's smuggling network; Veya and Maris want to escape with it.","conflict":"Veya's stubbornness leads her to go back for her notes, nearly getting them caught, and Kael hesitates when he sees her, torn between admiration and need.","outcome":"They escape, but Kael captures a copy of one chart panel, and Maris blames Veya for exposing her home.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_alliance"]},{"id":"scn_wardens_council","title":"The Wardens Divided","summary":"Veya presents the map to the Bridge Wardens at Emberroost and asks them to act on it. Maris, still angry, stands beside her. The Wardens argue over whether to share the map publicly.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the Wardens to reinforce the bridges the map marks as failing.","conflict":"Veya refuses to concede an error in her own reading of one span, and Maris's distrust nearly turns the Wardens against her.","outcome":"The Wardens agree to reinforce only one route unless the full map is made public, forcing Veya to choose between hoarding and sharing.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_raid"]},{"id":"scn_kael_closes_in","title":"The Last Stable Route","summary":"Using the captured chart panel, Kael seizes the toll gate on the one stable route, trapping merchants and forge-island supply convoys at Mistral Docks.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to lock in the Cartel's monopoly on the last stable route.","conflict":"The panel reveals the route is about to fail, and his equation of price with worth blinds him to the warning.","outcome":"Kael commits Cartel ships and toll-masters to the doomed route and sends word to Veya demanding the full map at the docks.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_raid"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Fall of the Span","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_veya_decides","title":"Sharing the Truth","summary":"Veya admits her earlier misreading to Maris and the Wardens and agrees to copy the full map for every isle. She chooses to bring it to the docks herself.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to publish the map so no single faction controls it.","conflict":"Her pride and fear of becoming like the Cartel leaders battle her need for recognition, and Maris must decide whether to trust her again.","outcome":"Veya makes copies for the academy and Maris, and Maris agrees to guide her through her corridors to the docks.","depends_on":["scn_wardens_council","scn_kael_closes_in"]},{"id":"scn_docks_confrontation","title":"The Docks at Drift","summary":"Veya confronts Kael at Mistral Docks, showing him that the route he holds will collapse. He must choose between seizing the map and heeding the warning.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to convince Kael to evacuate the route and release the map; Kael wants the original chart to control the remaining bridges.","conflict":"Kael's ruthlessness and belief in price over worth clash with Veya's openness, while Maris must slip her copies to merchants under the enforcers' eyes.","outcome":"The span begins to fail while the Cartel ships are still aboard, and Kael sees that his control has cost more than it gains.","depends_on":["scn_veya_decides"]},{"id":"scn_span_collapse","title":"Wind-Sight at the Breaking","summary":"As the skybridge breaks, Veya reads the wind to guide ships and merchants through a safe corridor. Maris leads a second group through her service paths, and Kael orders his toll-masters to open the gates.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"All three want to save the people on the failing route.","conflict":"Veya's reading is limited to what she can see in the wind, and Kael's open gates mean surrendering the monopoly he built.","outcome":"Most travellers are saved, the route is lost, and the map is copied across the isles, ending the Cartel's secret hold on it.","depends_on":["scn_docks_confrontation"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Shared Chart","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_reckoning","title":"Cost of Control","summary":"In the aftermath at Mistral Docks, Kael faces the Cartel's anger over the lost route and the open gates. He finds that his authority has fractured.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to account for the loss and decide what his role will be.","conflict":"The Cartel blames him for the lost route, and he cannot easily admit that Veya was right.","outcome":"Kael gives up his claim on the map and agrees to lower tolls on the routes that remain, in return for Veya's charts guiding the Cartel's ships.","depends_on":["scn_span_collapse"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Grain Across the Gap","summary":"Maris returns to The Hollow and uses the shared map to open new grain routes while the levy is renegotiated. She forgives Veya, slowly.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants The Hollow fed and the grain levy lifted; Veya wants to mend their trust.","conflict":"Maris's slow trust and reluctance to forgive make reconciliation difficult.","outcome":"Maris accepts Veya's friendship, and The Hollow's grain moves openly along routes both of them have charted.","depends_on":["scn_kael_reckoning"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_atlas","title":"The Map of All Isles","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya finishes the open atlas and places it where every isle can read it. She credits her mentor, Maris and the Wardens, and records the lost span as her own earlier error.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to complete her mentor's work and chart a safe route through the failing network.","conflict":"The temptation to claim sole credit pulls at her, but she names the others who helped.","outcome":"The atlas is shared with the whole archipelago, the isles prepare for further drift, and Veya has learned that truths are safer shared than hoarded.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_harvest"]}]}]}
