ks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to convince Kael to evacuate the route and release the map; Kael wants the original chart to control the remaining bridges.","conflict":"Kael's ruthlessness and belief in price over worth clash with Veya's openness, while Maris must slip her copies to merchants under the enforcers' eyes.","outcome":"The span begins to fail while the Cartel ships are still aboard, and Kael sees that his control has cost more than it gains.","depends_on":["scn_veya_decides"]},{"id":"scn_span_collapse","title":"Wind-Sight at the Breaking","summary":"As the skybridge breaks, Veya reads the wind to guide ships and merchants through a safe corridor. Maris leads a second group through her service paths, and Kael orders his toll-masters to open the gates.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"All three want to save the people on the failing route.","conflict":"Veya's reading is limited to what she can see in the wind, and Kael's open gates mean surrendering the monopoly he built.","outcome":"Most travellers are saved, the route is lost, and the map is copied across the isles, ending the Cartel's secret hold on it.","depends_on":["scn_docks_confrontation"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Shared Chart","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_reckoning","title":"Cost of Control","summary":"In the aftermath at Mistral Docks, Kael faces the Cartel's anger over the lost route and the open gates. He finds that his authority has fractured.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to account for the loss and decide what his role will be.","conflict":"The Cartel blames him for the lost route, and he cannot easily admit that Veya was right.","outcome":"Kael gives up his claim on the map and agrees to lower tolls on the routes that remain, in return for Veya's charts guiding the Cartel's ships.","depends_on":["scn_span_collapse"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Grain Across the Gap","summary":"Maris returns to The Hollow and uses the shared map to open new grain routes while the levy is renegotiated. She forgives Veya, slowly.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants The Hollow fed and the grain levy lifted; Veya wants to mend their trust.","conflict":"Maris's slow trust and reluctance to forgive make reconciliation difficult.","outcome":"Maris accepts Veya's friendship, and The Hollow's grain moves openly along routes both of them have charted.","depends_on":["scn_kael_reckoning"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_atlas","title":"The Map of All Isles","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya finishes the open atlas and places it where every isle can read it. She credits her mentor, Maris and the Wardens, and records the lost span as her own earlier error.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to complete her mentor's work and chart a safe route through the failing network.","conflict":"The temptation to claim sole credit pulls at her, but she names the others who helped.","outcome":"The atlas is shared with the whole archipelago, the isles prepare for further drift, and Veya has learned that truths are safer shared than hoarded.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_harvest"]}]}]}
