{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Bridge That Is and Is Not","logline":"As the skybridge network fails and the Drift Cartel moves to seize the last stable routes, a stubborn cartographer and a ruthless toll-master must decide whether the central skybridge will be held, surrendered, or both, and every choice comes with a cost for the isles that depend on it.","theme":"Truth and control cannot be held by one hand alone","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Fading Lines","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_charting_the_fracture","title":"Charting the Fracture","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya reads the wind and finds the central skybridge is failing and also still bearing traffic. Her instruments and her wind-sight give contradictory readings that she cannot explain away.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Chart a safe route through the breaking skybridge network, starting with the central skybridge.","conflict":"Her readings show the central skybridge both straining toward collapse and holding steady. Her stubbornness stops her from admitting the instruments might be right.","outcome":"Veya records the contradiction as proof of her late mentor's theory that the isles are drifting apart. She resolves to take the charts to the Wardens."},{"id":"scn_kael_tightens_the_toll","title":"Kael Tightens the Toll","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael learns that a cartographer is mapping the failing bridges. He sets the Cartel's toll on the central skybridge to the maximum while he builds a plan to seize the stable routes.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Seize the last stable skybridge routes before the bridges collapse.","conflict":"The Wardens accuse him of sabotaging forge-island supplies, and he admires Veya's skill while knowing her charts threaten his monopoly.","outcome":"Kael sends enforcers to find Veya and obtain her charts, and he raises the toll on the central skybridge.","depends_on":["scn_charting_the_fracture"]},{"id":"scn_the_grain_that_crosses","title":"The Grain That Crosses","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris hides a grain shipment from the Cartel levy and sees that enforcers are closing on her routes. She gets word that a cartographer is travelling the isles.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Smuggle enough grain to keep The Hollow fed through the crisis.","conflict":"The Cartel's enforcers watch the central skybridge, the only dependable crossing for her grain, and her slow trust leaves her with no one to turn to.","outcome":"Maris decides to look for a cartographer who might know safe crossings, and she sets out for Silverspine."}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Weight on the Weave","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_secret_paths_for_wind_knowledge","title":"Secret Paths for Wind Knowledge","summary":"At Silverspine, Maris finds Veya. They trade Veya's wind-current knowledge for Maris's unmapped service corridors, and together they see that the central skybridge can be crossed safely only by moving along its edge corridors.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to confirm her chart with ground-level routes, and Maris wants a safe crossing for her grain.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya's motives. Veya's wish for recognition makes her reluctant to share her charts freely.","outcome":"They form an alliance and agree to test the corridors together, leaving a cache of Veya's charts at the Academy.","depends_on":["scn_charting_the_fracture","scn_the_grain_that_crosses"]},{"id":"scn_the_wardens_forge","title":"The Wardens' Forge","summary":"Veya and Maris travel to Emberroost, where Bridge Wardens braid cloudstone cable. Veya presents her charts. The Wardens confirm the central skybridge cannot be reinforced in time, and they accuse the Cartel of withholding cable supplies.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Persuade the Wardens to act on the charts and reinforce the central skybridge.","conflict":"The Wardens will not move without proof, and Veya cannot admit that her first chart contained an error. The forge's open pits remind everyone that a single spark can sever a bridge.","outcome":"The Wardens lend Veya a braided cable sample and ask her to survey the central span in person, though doubts about her error remain.","depends_on":["scn_secret_paths_for_wind_knowledge"]},{"id":"scn_the_toll_masters_offer","title":"The Toll-Master's Offer","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael intercepts Veya and Maris and offers to buy the charts with cancelled wind-debt for The Hollow. He is charming but demands exclusive control, and Maris is tempted by the deal for her people.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants the charts under Cartel control, and Veya wants to leave with them intact.","conflict":"Maris's loyalty to home pulls her toward accepting. Veya's pride and Kael's belief that price equals worth bring the old rivalry back, and each sees the other's skill clearly.","outcome":"Veya refuses and Maris stays with her, though the refusal costs them: Kael's enforcers seal the docks and the pair escape along a service corridor Maris knows.","depends_on":["scn_the_wardens_forge"]},{"id":"scn_the_harvest_of_the_hollow","title":"The Harvest of the Hollow","summary":"Veya and Maris reach The Hollow and use the windmill corridors to move grain and hide the charts. Veya reads the wind and discovers that the bridge's readings are tied to which choices are being made about it, and she is forced to admit her first chart was wrong.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Keep The Hollow fed and use the safe corridors to check Veya's revised chart.","conflict":"Maris is angry that Veya's error nearly cost lives, and trust between them breaks. Veya must overcome her inability to admit she is wrong.","outcome":"Veya admits the mistake aloud, and Maris reluctantly forgives her. They decide to share the revised chart openly rather than hide it, and they head for the central skybridge.","depends_on":["scn_the_toll_masters_offer"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Bridge That Is and Is Not","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_standoff_on_the_span","title":"Standoff on the Span","summary":"On the central skybridge Veya and Kael meet. The span is audibly failing. Kael has arrived to claim the last stable route, and Veya has arrived to guide people off the bridge. The Cartel has barred the crossing.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to chart and open a safe crossing, and Kael wants to seize the span before it falls.","conflict":"Kael's enforcers hold the toll gate. Veya can prove the bridge is both failing and holding only if people choose to cross by the edge corridors. Kael's hold on the toll gate makes that crossing impossible.","outcome":"Kael sees that holding the gate will cost more lives than it earns and that he has no way to control a bridge that depends on shared choice.","depends_on":["scn_the_harvest_of_the_hollow"]},{"id":"scn_the_choice","title":"The Choice","summary":"Veya publishes her charts to all, and Kael lifts the toll. Maris leads crowds along her service corridors. The central span collapses where it was cut and stays standing where it was crossed together, so it both falls and holds.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Get everyone across the central skybridge by choosing to share the knowledge and the cost.","conflict":"Kael must give up the monopoly he spent his career building, Veya must give up the sole credit for her discovery, and Maris must trust strangers with her hidden routes.","outcome":"The bridge falls and holds at once: the main span is lost, but the edge corridors survive as a shared crossing, and nobody is stranded.","depends_on":["scn_standoff_on_the_span"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What Remains Standing","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_cost_of_control","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"Back at Mistral Docks, Kael pays the Cartel's wind-debt for the failed monopoly, gives up the toll-master's seat, and opens the ledgers to the Wardens. He admits to Veya that control cost more than it gained.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to settle the consequences of the collapse and decide what his skill is for.","conflict":"The Cartel's princes want him to answer for the lost monopoly, and he must face that price is not worth.","outcome":"Kael surrenders his monopoly and agrees to repay the wind-debt in labour alongside the Wardens, and the toll war cools.","depends_on":["scn_the_choice"]},{"id":"scn_a_map_for_everyone","title":"A Map for Everyone","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya adds Maris's corridors to the public charts and credits her ally and her late mentor. The isles keep drifting apart, but the network of shared crossings holds.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to finish the shared chart of the new crossings and share it with all isles.","conflict":"Some Academy scholars want the charts guarded, and Maris must decide whether to reveal her hidden corridors permanently.","outcome":"Veya learns that some truths are safer shared than hoarded, and Maris chooses to open her routes for the good of the archipelago.","depends_on":["scn_the_choice","scn_the_cost_of_control"]},{"id":"scn_the_still_hollow","title":"The Still Hollow","summary":"In The Hollow, windmills turn again as grain crosses by the shared edge corridors without a levy. Maris sits with Veya and Kael, who has come to repay his debt in labour, and the three watch the wind carry the drifting isles.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Restore The Hollow's grain trade and begin repairing trust.","conflict":"Maris still struggles to forgive Kael, and he must work without expecting thanks.","outcome":"Maris realises that hiding can be as brave as standing still and that sharing can be braver, and the three accept an uneasy peace as the isles drift on.","depends_on":["scn_a_map_for_everyone"]}]}]}
